 "standard_text": "Expand two binomials; factorise quadratic expressions; factorise the difference of two squares. (summary of the NERDC JSS 3 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 3 maths worksheets on quadratics: expanding two brackets, perfect squares, factorising x² + bx + c and the difference of two squares. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "x² + bx + c = (x + p)(x + q)",
 "key_sub": "p + q = b and pq = c",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>(x + 3)(x + 4) = x² + 7x + 12.</li><li>To factorise x² + bx + c, find two numbers that multiply to c and add to b.</li><li>The difference of two squares: a² − b² = (a + b)(a − b).</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x² − x − 12</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>−4 × 3 = −12, −4 + 3 = −1</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: (x − 4)(x + 3)</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x² − 49</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Difference of two squares</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: (x + 7)(x − 7)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Getting the signs wrong</td><td>Check by expanding.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting the middle term</td><td>(x + 3)² = x² + 6x + 9.</td></tr><tr><td>Stopping at a common factor</td><td>Factorise fully.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is a quadratic?",
   "a": "An expression with x² as the highest power."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I check?",
   "a": "Multiply the brackets back out."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can every quadratic be factorised?",
   "a": "Not with whole numbers."
  }
